## Summary

Bootstrap `StarLine Telemetry for Home Assistant` as a read-only custom integration plus dashboard workspace.

### Integration
- official StarLine Open API authentication and device discovery;
- one coordinated `/json/v3/device/{device_id}/data` snapshot per vehicle;
- quota-aware polling with a 180 s minimum and ~800 device-data requests/day account budget;
- sensor, binary_sensor and GPS device_tracker platforms;
- `ConfigEntry.runtime_data` and current Home Assistant 2026.x APIs;
- redacted diagnostics;
- English and Russian translations.

### Safety boundary
- no `/set_param` implementation;
- no `/async` vehicle command implementation;
- no arm/disarm, engine, heater or settings writes;
- dashboard contract explicitly contains `commands: []`.

### Dashboard
- semantic `CONTRACT_GENERATED_UI` contract;
- fixed `Status → Control → Diagnostics` architecture;
- control section is informational/read-only.

### Validation
- Python syntax, JSON and YAML were validated locally;
- hassfest and HACS validation workflows are included.

Version baseline: `0.1.0`.

## Scope

Complete the Stage 0-D.2 generic realtime control-channel primitive defined by `docs/REALTIME_CONTROL_SPSC_CHANNEL.md`.

## Production behavior
- one serialized producer / one realtime consumer;
- compile-time fixed capacity;
- bounded trivially-copyable ST-owned value messages;
- exact FIFO ordering;
- full => explicit reject, never overwrite/drop/coalesce;
- empty => explicit bounded result;
- release/acquire publication ordering;
- no allocation, locks, waits, retry loops, logging, Project traversal, or arbitrary realtime destruction;
- uint64 producer/consumer sequence counters with modular distance;
- physical ring indices are maintained independently from sequence counters so `UINT64_MAX -> 0` wrap cannot alias slots for non-power-of-two capacities.

## Verification
New strict-warning CTest covers:
- lock-free sequence atomics and message constraints;
- empty behavior without output fabrication;
- exact-capacity fill and full rejection;
- FIFO preservation and no-overwrite;
- one-slot release/reuse;
- capacity-one operation;
- non-power-of-two capacity across real uint64 sequence wrap;
- 1000 deterministic fill/full/drain/empty cycles;
- noexcept push/pop.

